  "issue": {
    "body": "For quite a while now we've no longer documented the decorator-style for routing.\r\n\r\n*We document this style of routing configuration...*\r\n\r\n```python\r\ndef homepage(request):\r\n    ...\r\n\r\nroutes = [\r\n    Route('/', homepage),\r\n]\r\n\r\napp = Starlette(routes=routes)\r\n```\r\n\r\n*We no longer document this...*\r\n\r\n```python\r\napp = Starlette()\r\n\r\n@app.route(\"/\")\r\ndef homepage(request):\r\n    ...\r\n```\r\n\r\nHowever several of our test cases still continue to use the old style, which is a bit inconsistent.\r\n\r\nThe same also applies to `app.add_middleware` vs. `app = Starlette(..., middleware=...)`.\r\n\r\nWe could do with a bit of clean-up here.\r\n\r\n* Drop routing decorators in test cases.\r\n* Drop `.add_middleware` in test cases.\r\n* Add docstrings to the now undocumented API - \"We no longer document this decorator style API, and its usage is discouraged\"\r\n\r\nFor splitting this into individual chunks I'd probably suggest...\r\n\r\n* A pull request for the docstrings change.\r\n* Several pull requests for the test case change. Each pull request should only affect one file.",
    "body_last_edited_at": null,
    "closed_at": "2022-02-11T09:46:02Z",
